    {
      "number": 13,
      "id": "I_kwDOU6OITc8AAAABYaftVw",
      "title": "How persistent state has impact on network operation or robust metrics?",
      "url": "https://github.com/billwuqin/Agent-Benchmarking/issues/13",
      "state": "OPEN",
      "author": "billwuqin",
      "authorAssociation": "OWNER",
      "assignees": [],
      "labels": [],
      "body": "From Yhasa, draft-khandelwal-bmwg-agent-memory-integrity author:\nThe only thing I would still ask Luis to keep is small and has nothing to do with security. Section 4 already says to document persistent state across runs. That state is something the agent reads at the start of every episode, so it should be treated like the model version and the prompt template: pin it in 5.2 so the run can be repeated, and list it in 6.4 with the other inputs that get perturbed. How you perturb it is a separate question, and my draft is one answer, but the main thing is that the starting state counts as an input.",
      "createdAt": "2026-10-19T23:46:48Z",
      "updatedAt": "2026-10-19T23:46:48Z",
      "closedAt": null,
      "comments": []
    }
  ],
